On Fri, Oct 7, 2016 at 9:10 AM, selpahi <seladwa@gmx.de> wrote:

>
> https://solpahi.wordpress.com/2016/09/25/a-simpler-quantifier-logic/


Nice. I agree with most of it, although I'm not too sure yet what I think
about ro and su'o becoming ro'oi and su'oi.

Have you thought about "su'e"? Presumably it should pattern with "ru'o",
not with "ro'oi", so the su'o/su'e symmetry would be broken if su'o becomes
su'oi.

Would "no" become "no'oi" as well?

We should also have explicit definitions for me'i, za'u, da'a, so'a, so'e,
etc since they all admit more than one pluralification, but I'm guessing
they would all follow the "ru'o" pattern as well.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

